# Lab 20 Experiment 1: Package and provider-source Registration lookup
#
# Run one request at a time with the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Keep all real values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<A365-Registry-Experiment-client-id>
# A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID=<leave-empty-until-step-4>
# A365_SAMPLE_SOURCE_AGENT_ID_PATH=<provider-source-id-encoded-for-one-path-segment>
#
# Never commit .env, response files, access tokens, package IDs, agent names,
# tenant IDs, client IDs, endpoints, or other identifiers.
#
# If Send Request appears to do nothing, confirm that .env exists in the
# Lab 20 root and contains non-placeholder values for A365_TENANT_ID and
# A365_CLIENT_ID.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@samplePackageId = {{$dotenv A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID}}
@sampleSourceAgentIdPath = {{$dotenv A365_SAMPLE_SOURCE_AGENT_ID_PATH}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@experimentScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Step 1 - Start delegated device-code authentication
#
# URL:
#   POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
#
# Request:
#   Uses the public-client application and requests only
#   CopilotPackages.Read.All plus offline_access.
#
# Expected response:
#   HTTP 200
#   {
#     "user_code": "<short-lived-code>",
#     "device_code": "<short-lived-device-code>",
#     "verification_uri": "https://microsoft.com/devicelogin",
#     "expires_in": 900,
#     "interval": 5,
#     "message": "..."
#   }
#
# Do not copy either code into chat or tracked evidence.

# @name startDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{experimentScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 2 - Complete sign-in
#
# This step has no HTTP request in this file.
#
# 1. Read verification_uri and user_code from the Step 1 response.
# 2. Open verification_uri locally.
# 3. Enter user_code.
# 4. Sign in as the approved user.
# 5. Return here and run Step 3.

###############################################################################
# Step 3 - Exchange the device code for a Graph access token
#
# URL:
#   POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{tenant-id}/oauth2/v2.0/token
#
# Request:
#   Reuses device_code directly from the named Step 1 response.
#
# Expected success response:
#   HTTP 200
#   {
#     "token_type": "Bearer",
#     "scope": "... CopilotPackages.Read.All ...",
#     "expires_in": 3599,
#     "access_token": "<sensitive-token>",
#     "refresh_token": "<sensitive-token>"
#   }
#
# If sign-in is not complete, the response can be HTTP 400 with:
#   "error": "authorization_pending"
#
# Complete Step 2, wait for the configured interval, and run Step 3 again.
# Never save or share the token response.

# @name exchangeDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{startDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step 4 - List all packages in the tenant
#
# URL:
#   GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
#
# Request:
#   Read-only. Requires delegated CopilotPackages.Read.All.
#
# Expected response:
#   HTTP 200
#   {
#     "value": [
#       {
#         "id": "P_<package-id>",
#         "displayName": "<agent-name>",
#         "type": "<package-type>",
#         "platform": "<source-platform>",
#         "assetId": "<asset-id>",
#         "isBlocked": false,
#         "lastModifiedDateTime": "<timestamp>"
#       }
#     ],
#     "@odata.nextLink": "<present only when another page exists>"
#   }
#
# In the local response:
# 1. Find one already-approved, non-production GCP Registry Sync sample.
# 2. Copy only its package id into A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID in the ignored .env.
# 3. Follow @odata.nextLink if the response is paginated.
#
# Do not assume package id, assetId, or displayName is an Agent Registration ID.

# @name listPackages
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{exchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Step 5 - Get details for the selected package
#
# URL:
#   GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{id}
#
# Request:
#   Uses exactly the package ID placed in A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID after Step 4.
#   It does not list packages again and does not match by name.
#
# Expected response:
#   HTTP 200 with one copilotPackageDetail object:
#   {
#     "id": "P_<same-package-id>",
#     "displayName": "<agent-name>",
#     "type": "<package-type>",
#     "platform": "<source-platform>",
#     "assetId": "<asset-id>",
#     "elementDetails": [ ... ]
#   }
#
# Record only whether these fields are present, absent, or undocumented:
# - id
# - platform
# - assetId
# - owner / ownerIds
# - sourceAgentId
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId
# - agentIdentityId
# - managedByAppId
# - originatingStore
#
# The documented package-detail example does not establish that identity or
# Agent Registration fields are part of this resource. The live response is
# the observation; absence must not be rewritten as "unsupported."
#
# SAVE REQUIRED:
# ../../evidence/experiments/01-package-registration-lookup/package-details.json
#
# Copy the top-level Package ID to A365_SAMPLE_PACKAGE_ID. Copy the nested
# provider SourceAgentId to A365_SAMPLE_SOURCE_AGENT_ID_PATH after encoding it
# for one URL path segment.

# @name getSelectedPackage
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{samplePackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###
###############################################################################
# Step 6.1 - Try the Package ID as a Registration ID
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: status and safe error class only. The documented Registration
# GET expects a Registration ID, so this is a bounded negative probe.

# @name getRegistrationUsingPackageIdNegativeProbe
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{samplePackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{exchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json


###
###############################################################################
# Step 6.2 - Try the provider source ID as a Registration ID
#
# Put the exact provider SourceAgentId into one URL path segment. If the
# observed source already contains percent escapes, encode each percent sign
# for the path, for example %2f becomes %252f.
#
# SAVE REQUIRED: status and safe error class only.

# @name getRegistrationUsingProviderSourceIdNegativeProbe
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{sampleSourceAgentIdPath}}
Authorization: ******
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Optional inventory-only convenience query
#
# Do not use this filter as proof that every returned GoogleVertexAI Package
# came from Registry Sync.

# @name listGoogleVertexPackages
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages?$filter=platform eq 'GoogleVertexAI'
Authorization: Bearer {{exchangeDeviceCode.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###############################################################################
# Stop after Step 6
#
# Do not create a Blueprint, Agent Identity, or Registration, and do not PATCH
# anything. Package IDs, provider source IDs, and Agent Registration IDs remain
# different identifier classes.

###############################################################################
# Step 7 - Documented identifier boundary (no request)
#
# Current first-party documentation exposes:
#
# Inventory:
#   GET /v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
#   GET /v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{package-id}
#
# Registration lifecycle:
#   POST   /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
#   GET    /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{registration-id}
#   PATCH  /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{registration-id}
#   DELETE /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{registration-id}
#
# It does not document:
# - a list operation for agentRegistrations;
# - a lookup by package ID or third-party source agent ID;
# - a package-to-agentRegistration ID field; or
# - that the package ID can be used as a registration ID.
#
# Observed for the selected GCP Connected Platform package:
# - package details are readable;
# - the third-party source agent ID exists only in nested platform metadata;
# - no Blueprint ID is present;
# - the Entra Agent ID value is null;
# - no documented Agent Registration ID is exposed.
#
# Therefore there is no supported HTTP request to place here for the proposed
# registration PATCH target. Do not guess an ID or call the PATCH endpoint.
